{{Quote|My name, for the record, is ''Coburn Sear'' of ''Quarzite''. I am a colonel of the Confederacy of Independent Systems&hellip;and I do not seek the mercy of tyrants. Rather, I seek&hellip;to take those tyrants with me.|Colonel Coburn Sear, to Caleb Dume|<ref name="Kanan 11">[[Kanan 11|''Kanan'' 11]]</ref>}}
'''Colonel''' ('''Col.''') was a [[military rank]] that was common to most militaries throughout [[the galaxy]]. It was generally below the rank of [[general]] and above the ranks of [[major]] and [[commander]]. The rank itself was relatively high in the greater chain of command.

==Description==
Colonel, abbreviated to Col. when addressing an individual of the station,<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> was a [[military rank]] used by [[officer]]s in the armed forces of various factions throughout [[Timeline of galactic history|galactic history]], as well as [[Law enforcement agency|law enforcement and intelligence agencies]].<ref name="Tarkin" /> The rank of colonel was below that of [[Brigadier General|brigadier general]]<ref name="HC 79">{{HelmetCollectionCite|79|Databank A-Z}}</ref> and above a [[Lieutenant Colonel|lieutenant colonel]].<ref name="Lords of the Sith">''[[Lords of the Sith]]''</ref> The title of [[High Colonel]] also existed.<ref name="Shadow of the Sith">''[[Shadow of the Sith]]''</ref>

==History==
[[File:Datoo_-_SW_Card_Trader.png|thumb|left|180px|Erich S. Datoo, a Colonel in the First Order]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], both the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]<ref name="Kanan 9">[[Kanan 9|''Kanan'' 9]]</ref> and the [[Galactic Republic]] utilized the rank of colonel.<ref name="Secret Weapons" /> An example of each included the Confederacy's Colonel [[Coburn Sear]], who led [[Separatist Droid Army]] forces during the [[Third Battle of Mygeeto]].<ref name="Kanan 9" /> The Republic Colonel [[Meebur Gascon]] served as a strategist within [[Republic High Command]]. During the war, he commanded the [[droid]] unit [[D-Squad]] on a [[Mission to steal a Separatist encryption module|mission]] to steal a [[Encryption module|Separatist encryption module]].<ref name="Secret Weapons" />

The Republic's successor government, the [[Galactic Empire]], utilized the officer rank in various capacities during the [[Imperial Era]]. It was used by both the [[Imperial Army]],<ref name="Vader 13">[[Darth Vader (2017) 13|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 13]]</ref> the [[Imperial Starfighter Corps]],<ref name="Alphabet Squadron">[[Alphabet Squadron (novel)|''Alphabet Squadron'']]</ref> and the [[Imperial Security Bureau]].<ref name="Tarkin" /> 

